**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests`

**How to implement.** The Details bay names a band's material through the scene's live materials store, not through the code seed (001 §R: the code seed values go; .spec-md §0.1 `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` row). The colour maps keep reading `MaterialIds` (the S1.7 brief: Schematic.fs and the colour map keep the well-known ids): `bandColors` and `Schematic.fs`'s curated colours are unchanged, except that the curated map's doc keys it by `MaterialIds` and no longer names `MaterialLibrary.builtInEntries`. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) the private `materialLibrary` (`= MaterialLibrary.standard`, the composition-root comment above it included) is deleted; (2) `MaterialId.bandDisplayName` becomes `member private materialId.bandDisplayName (materials : MaterialLibrary.MaterialProxy) : string`: the name of `materials.tryGetMaterial materialId`'s entry, or the id's GUID string when the store holds none or the lookup fails, so an unknown id still labels its band as today; (3) `Sample.bandsState` becomes `member s.bandsState (materials : MaterialLibrary.MaterialProxy) : LayerBandsControls.LayerBandsControlsState` and passes the store to each band; (4) `detailsState` passes `model.materials`. The docs say the names come from the materials store in no more words. No cache and no second lookup is added. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainWorkbenchTests.fs`: `sampleBandsState collapses a period group to x-N bands (the Details-bay shape)` reads `(BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.multilayerQwId).bandsState (BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()).materials`, with its assertions unchanged, and the class gains `the band view names each band's material through the materials store it is given`: over the fixture's fresh materials store the quarter-wave stack's three band labels start with `Transparent glass (n = 1.52)`, `Vacuum` and `Transparent glass (n = 1.52)`, and over an empty `MaterialProxy.createInMemoryEmpty (fun _ -> []) VersionsInUse.empty` each label starts with its material's GUID string.

**Acceptance.** After the switch, `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs` MUST NOT name `MaterialLibrary.standard`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `sampleBandsState collapses a period group to x-N bands (the Details-bay shape)` and `the band view names each band's material through the materials store it is given`; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.
